      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me analyze the logic before writing the improved version:\n\n- `ofTaiSeconds(-1660, -1660)` normalizes: -1660 nanos borrows 1 second → stored as (-1661s, 999_998_340ns)\n- `minus(Duration.ZERO)` returns `this` (same-instance optimization)\n- The test verifies both the normalization and the identity-return optimizationThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces opaque auto-generated variable names (`taiInstant0`, `taiInstant1`, `duration0`) with descriptive names (`instantWithNegativeNanos`, `resultAfterSubtractingZero`) and adds comments explaining the nano normalization logic and the identity-return optimization in `minus(Duration.ZERO)`."
